      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, so our production db is a total mess right now lol. there's just so much junk and redundant data everywhere, it's making everything super slow and hard to manage. i need to clean it up by moving to 3nf but i'm kinda stuck on how to actually handle the transitive dependencies without breaking stuff. can u walk me through how to identify them and how the actual table splitting works?",
